{"parentUuid":"3278215a-a558-4142-a778-6c79d53ba005","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"30d26bdd-0c1f-4886-9efc-825c4997ccbc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0175U66kHT1xuqDG3XyRr61i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: project-open-studio-opencode-audit\n3\tdescription: Open-Studio project — folding opencode + open-notebook into memo-ray + Benny; Phase 1 (opencode audited in memo-ray) is done\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: c9e03e56-5425-4e3d-8d0c-40d1a1b8d58d\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t**Open-Studio** is a project (started 2026-06-19) to fold two OSS tools into the existing\n11\tbinary16 stack instead of building those slices from scratch: **opencode** (sst/opencode,\n12\tlocal coding agent) and **open-notebook** (lfnovo, open NotebookLM). Plan file:\n13\t`~/.claude/plans/i-was-thinking-of-hazy-platypus.md`. Decisions: extend memo-ray + prime-silo\n14\tin place (no new repo); make memo-ray the universal local-agent audit layer; make Benny a\n15\tfloating \"dog\" (phased: reskin the in-browser `_core/onscreen_agent/` overlay → standalone\n16\talways-on-top desktop-pet window). See [[project-binary16-app-registry]], [[benny-self-awareness-and-bridge-files]].\n17\t\n18\t**memo-ray audit pattern** (how Claude/Gemini are \"audited\" — and now opencode too): four seams in\n19\t`memo-ray/agent-os-dashboard/server`: (1) `memoray.config.js` paths (but the *runtime* config is\n20\tthe auto-generated `~/.memoray/memoray.config.js` from `lib/config.js`+`lib/detector.js`, NOT the\n21\trepo file); (2) `lib/detector.js` PROBE_LISTS/GUIDES + singleKeys/arrayKeys; (3) `parsers/<agent>Parser.js`\n22\t→ entities; (4) `/api/system/capabilities` reads each agent's tools/permission grants = the audit.\n23\tEntities: `{id,type,agent,timestamp,content,metadata,parent_id,children_ids}`, MD5 ids, stored as\n24\tone JSON file each under `~/.memoray/data/entities/`. Overview agent split keys off `agent