a `/api/llm/{p}/start|stop`),\nshows running models, lets you set the master default + per-role model, shows what each role resolves to. Uses\n`/llm/status` (provider→{running,models.data,name,port,can_start/stop}) for the model dropdowns.\n\nAll synced into the running exe: shell files → `…/win-unpacked/resources/app/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/`,\nbackend → `…/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/api/llm_routes.py` (+ models.py earlier). Verified: node --check, py_compile,\nbundled-python import of server + llm_routes endpoints OK. Runtime was DOWN at sync time (app closed, :8005 not\nlistening) → loads on next exe launch. NOT yet clicked through live.\n\n**STATUS: ingestion vectors verified live; routing bug fixed; Agents config screen built + bundled. Next exe\nlaunch: open Bridge→Agents, set graph_synthesis to lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat, re-ingest → triples populate.**\nSee [[project-open-studio-opencode-audit]].","originalFile":"---\nname: prime-silo-rag-ingestion-fix\ndescription: \"Prime-Silo document ingestion was broken — embedding-fn mismatch, hollow success, no triples; fixed + RAG-chat surfaced\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 50d606f7-67d3-4645-8504-2cafd7318b4d\n---\n\n**Prime-Silo RAG ingestion fix (started 2026-06-20).** User reported \"document ingestion not working\"\nand \"Benny studio features missing.\" Root causes found in `prime-silo/runtime/benny`:\n\n1. **Embedding-function split (the killer).** The `\"knowledge\"` Chroma collection was opened two ways:\n   `tools/knowledge.py` used `LocalEmbeddingFunction()` (768-dim HTTP → LM Studio/Lemonade/Ollama),\n   but `rag_routes.py` (ingest/query/chat/status), `core/adaptive_rag.py`, `api/graph_routes.py`,\n   `api/studio_executor.py` used bare `get_or_create_collection(\"knowledge\")` → Chroma's networked ONNX\n   `DefaultEmbeddingFunction` (384-dim, needs onnxruntime + a download — absent in the bundled/offline\n   runtime). So ingest's `collection.add` r