ic-embed-text-v1.5`). (4) Chroma 1.5.9 \"embedding function conflict:\npersisted: default\": old collection built with Chroma's default EF → made `get_knowledge_collection` drop+recreate\non conflict, and gave `LocalEmbeddingFunction` `name()/get_config()/build_from_config()` so future opens don't\nconflict. Result: re-ingest → 190 chunks embed cleanly, NO LM Studio error, NO EF conflict.\n\n**REMAINING = model choice, not code. `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` is a REASONING model**: with max_tokens 1024 it\nemits valid triple JSON but takes ~64s for a trivial sentence (burns ~234 reasoning tokens first), and on large\ndoc chunks the reasoning can exceed the budget → empty `content` (finish:length) → 0 triples → graph stays empty.\nThe other LM Studio models (`qwen/qwen3-coder-30b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`) FAIL TO LOAD (\"Engine protocol startup\naborted\" — memory pressure with gemma loaded). **FIX FOR USER (via the new Bridge→Agents screen):** assign\n`graph_synthesis` (and `chat`) to a non-reasoning instruct model — ideally start **Lemonade** (was down) and use\n**Qwen3-8B-Hybrid** (small/fast/NPU, won't fight gemma for GPU), or load a light instruct model in LM Studio.\n\n**STATUS: every code bug fixed + verified live (vectors=190, embeddings auto-detect, routing local+configurable,\nself-healing collection). Graph triples blocked only by reasoning-model slowness/empty-output — user picks a\nbetter graph_synthesis model in Bridge→Agents.** See [[project-open-studio-opencode-audit]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2545,"cache_read_input_tokens":364129,"output_tokens":3461,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2545,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":3461,"cache_read_input_tok