vider scan).\n(3) LM Studio \"No models loaded\": embeddings hardcoded `nomic-embed-text-v1-GGUF` (Lemonade's name; Lemonade was\nDOWN) → added `_resolve_embedding_model` in embeddings.py that queries provider `/models` and picks an id\ncontaining \"embed\" (→ `text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5`). (4) Chroma 1.5.9 \"embedding function conflict:\npersisted: default\": old collection built with Chroma's default EF → made `get_knowledge_collection` drop+recreate\non conflict, and gave `LocalEmbeddingFunction` `name()/get_config()/build_from_config()` so future opens don't\nconflict. Result: re-ingest → 190 chunks embed cleanly, NO LM Studio error, NO EF conflict.\n\n**REMAINING = model choice, not code. `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` is a REASONING model**: with max_tokens 1024 it\nemits valid triple JSON but takes ~64s for a trivial sentence (burns ~234 reasoning tokens first), and on large\ndoc chunks the reasoning can exceed the budget → empty `content` (finish:length) → 0 triples → graph stays empty.\nThe other LM Studio models (`qwen/qwen3-coder-30b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`) FAIL TO LOAD (\"Engine protocol startup\naborted\" — memory pressure with gemma loaded). **FIX FOR USER (via the new Bridge→Agents screen):** assign\n`graph_synthesis` (and `chat`) to a non-reasoning instruct model — ideally start **Lemonade** (was down) and use\n**Qwen3-8B-Hybrid** (small/fast/NPU, won't fight gemma for GPU), or load a light instruct model in LM Studio.\n\n**STATUS: every code bug fixed + verified live (vectors=190, embeddings auto-detect, routing local+configurable,\nself-healing collection). Graph triples blocked only by reasoning-model slowness/empty-output — user picks a\nbetter graph_synthesis model in Bridge→Agents.** See [[project-open-studio-opencode-audit]].","originalFile":"---\nname: prime-silo-rag-ingestion-fix\ndescription: \"Prime-Silo document ingestion was broken — embedding-fn mismatch, hollow success, no triples; fixed + RAG-chat surfaced\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 50d606f7-67d3-4645-8504-2cafd7318b4d\n---\n\n**Prime-Silo RAG ingestion fix (started 2026-06-20).** User reported \"document ingestion not working\"\nand \"Benny studio features missing.\" Root causes found in `prime-silo/runtime/benny`:\n\n1. **Embedding-function split (the killer).** The `\"knowledge\"` Chroma collection was opened two ways:\n   `tools/knowledge.py` used `LocalEmbeddingFunction()` (768-dim HTTP → LM Studio/Lemonade/Ollama),\n   but `rag_routes.py` (ingest/query/chat/status), `core/adaptive_rag.py`, `api/graph_routes.py`,\n   `api/studio_executor.py` used bare `get_or_create_collection(\"knowledge\")` → Chroma's networked ONNX\n   `DefaultEmbeddingFunction` (384-dim, needs onnxruntime + a download — absent in the bundled/offline\n   runtime). So ingest's `collection.add` raised, was swallowed (rag_routes ~line 180), and the endpoint\n   still returned `status:\"completed\"` → hollow success, empty index. Plus 384-vs-768 dim mismatch when\n   tool + route paths touched the same collection.\n   **FIX:** added `get_knowledge_collection(client, name=\"knowledge\")` in `tools/knowledge.py` (always\n   attaches `LocalEmbeddingFunction()`); routed ALL call sites through it. `grep 'get_or_create_collection(\"knowledge\")'`\n   must return nothing.\n2. **No triples → empty graph.** Documents page's kg3d/synoptic_web reads Neo4j (`graph/kg3d/ontology.py`),\n   populated only by `deep_synthesis` (triple extraction). But Bridge `ingest()` posted `{workspace}` and\n   `deep_synthesis` defaults False → graph stayed empty though the chip promises triples.\n   **FIX:** `bridge.js ingest()` now sends `deep_synthesis:true`.\n3. **Silent failure.** Indexing/synthesis errors caught + reported as success.\n   **FIX:** ingest tracks per-file `indexed`/`error`, returns honest `status` ∈ completed /\n   completed_with_errors / failed + `indexed_files`/`failed_files`/`message`; added an **embedding-provider\n   preflight** (`get_embedding_sync(\"ping\")`; all-zeros → 503 \"start LM Studio/Lemonade/Ollama\").\n\n**Phase 2 started — surfaced RAG chat.** Backend has all surfaces (server.py registers Studio/Notebook/RAG/\nDeepProduce/AgentAmp/Pypes) but the Space-Agent shell only vendors a thin widget set + the Bridge cockpit\n(`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js`; the rich Benny React frontend is NOT vendored — only in\n`archive/benny/frontend/`). Added an \"Ask the docs\" box to the Documents panel (bridge.js `askDocs()` → POST\n`/rag/chat` semantic; view.html `.ps-bridge__ask`; bridge.css). Still missing from shell: Notebook node-chat,\nStudio node editor, Pypes drilldown UI, AgentAmp, Rationale-Hub wiki.\n\n**Arch reminder:** shell proxies `/api/runtime/*` → Benny FastAPI `127.0.0.1:8005` (`server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`,\nstrips `/api/runtime`, injects `X-Benny-API-Key`). Bundled runtime started by `packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js`.\n\n**Self-heal + deps (2026-06-20, follow-up — \"just run the exe\").** Added `heal_collection_dimension(client,\ncollection, name, probe_vec)` in `tools/knowledge.py`: canary-adds the 768-dim probe vec; on a dimensionality\nerror it `delete_collection` + recreates → **no manual chromadb cleanup needed**. Called in ingest right after\n`get_knowledge_collection`. Confirmed the runtime bundle already bakes every ingestion dep\n(`packaging/scripts/assemble-runtime-bundle.js` BUNDLE_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENTS: chromadb, PyMuPDF, pypdf,\nbeautifulsoup4, markdownify; embeddings use httpx) — and since the fix routes through the HTTP\n`LocalEmbeddingFunction`, **onnxruntime/sentence-transformers are NOT needed** (the old default-embedder\ndownload was the bug). The ONE thing not bundlable: an external embedding/LLM server (LM Studio :1234 /\nLemonade :13305 / Ollama) must be up — same prerequisite as chat/synthesis; preflight 503 says so clearly.\n\nCI note: prime-silo desktop gate (`release-desktop.yml`) runs only NODE tests; runtime's own\n`portable-safety.yml` runs only `tests/portability tests/safety` — so `tests/api/test_rag_routes.py` does NOT\ngate the exe. Tests updated anyway (success asserts indexed_files==1; +503-provider-down; +2 heal-helper unit\ntests) and pass `py_compile`; not executed live (no chromadb/fastapi interpreter on this machine).\n\n**LIVE RUN (2026-06-20, exe) — vectors OK, synthesis was misrouting to OpenAI.** Ran ingest in the built exe\n(run 08442161…, workspace default, FrolovRoutledge2024.pdf). Result: **vector ingestion WORKED** — 190 chunks\nin ChromaDB (embedding fix confirmed live, local embedder reached, no onnxruntime). But the **knowledge graph\nstayed empty (0 triples)**: every `graph_synthesis` LLM call failed \"Missing OPENAI_API_KEY\". Root cause = bug\nin `core/models.py::get_active_model`: the local-provider heartbeat probe built the models URL via\n`base_url.replace(\"/v1\",\"/models\")` which STRIPS the /v1 segment (LM Studio `:1234/v1` → `:1234/models`, a 404),\nso local chat models were never detected → `default` workspace leaked to `openai/gpt-4o` (no key in bundle).\nEmbeddings were unaffected (embeddings.py uses its own correct `/embeddings` path). **FIX:** probe URL =\n`base_url.rstrip('/')+'/models'`; and the global fallback now stays local (`lemonade/default`) unless online\nWITH an OPENAI_API_KEY. Verified LM Studio `:1234/v1/models` lists `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` → after restart the\nprobe resolves `lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat`. Fix applied to source AND hot-copied into the running bundle\n(`…/win-unpacked/resources/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/core/models.py`). **Runtime must be restarted (quit+relaunch\nthe exe) to load it**, then re-ingest → triples should populate. NOTE: provider probe order is ollama→lemonade→\nfastflowlm→lmstudio; lemonade/:13305 + ollama returned empty, lmstudio answered.\n\n**Agents management screen (2026-06-20) — single config surface for model routing.** User wanted Benny Studio's\nagent-management screen active in the shell so a