{"parentUuid":"7c47bad3-ab8b-4704-a5a7-ab0e29f8f2ed","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"95f3b60c-62ce-49ea-b79c-3ca2ce20ebe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019C3PRMSgExq5QCNduHvguw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: devops-pipeline\n3\tdescription: Build, test-package, and release the Prime-Silo desktop app (Space Agent). Use when asked to build the app, make a local/test build, package for Windows/macOS/Linux, cut a release, bump the version, or debug the release CI. Covers the Open-Studio companion services (opencode + open-notebook) bundling.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Prime-Silo DevOps pipeline\n7\t\n8\tPrime-Silo packages as an Electron desktop app (\"Space Agent\") via **electron-builder**.\n9\tTwo product layers ship together: the Space-Agent shell (Node server + browser UI, run\n10\tin-process) and the **Benny runtime** (Python + Neo4j + JRE) which is either bundled\n11\t(zero-install) or driven from an external `$BENNY_HOME`.\n12\t\n13\tAll commands run from the repo root: `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo`.\n14\t\n15\t## 0. One-time: install packaging deps\n16\t\n17\telectron + electron-builder live under `packaging/`. If `packaging/node_modules` is\n18\tmissing, run first:\n19\t```\n20\tnpm run install:packaging\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\t## 1. Build types (pick the lightest that proves what you need)\n24\t\n25\t| Goal | Command | Output | Notes |\n26\t|------|---------|--------|------|\n27\t| Fast shell-only test (validates main/tray/pet/UI changes) | `npm run desktop:pack` | `dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe` | **No** runtime bundle. Quick. Best for verifying desktop/main-process changes. |\n28\t| Zero-install local test (full runtime) | `npm run desktop:localtest` | same path, with bundled Python+Neo4j+JRE | Sets `PRIME_SILO_BUNDLE_RUNTIME=1`; **downloads hundreds of MB + runs pip** — slow first run. This is the artifact to validate before tagging. |\n29\t| Windows installer | `npm run package:desktop:windows` | NSIS installer in `dist/` | Full build. |\n30\t| All Windows arches | `npm run package:desktop:windows:all` | x64 + arm64 | |\n31\t| macOS / Linux | `npm run package:desktop:{macos,linux}[:all]` | dmg+zip / AppImage | Run on the target OS. |\n32\t\n33\tBuild internals: scripts under `packaging/scripts/` (`host-package.js`,\n34\t`build-local-test.js` → `desktop-builder.js`). `build.files` in `package.json` controls\n35\twhat ships — `packaging/desktop/**/*` is globbed, so new files there (e.g. `pet.js`,\n36\t`openstudio_services.js`) bundle automatically. `app/L1` and `app/L2` are excluded.\n37\t\n38\t### Verify a build\n39\t```\n40\tls \"dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe\"\n41\t# asar is disabled, so app files are browsable for spot-checks:\n42\tls \"dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/resources/app/packaging/desktop/\"\n43\t```\n44\tFor a zero-install build, follow the on-screen checklist `build-local-test.js` prints:\n45\tlaunch the exe → tray reaches **\"Benny runtime: running (bundled)\"** → in the Bridge,\n46\tDocuments ingest + Code 3D graph + Flows deep-produce all work with no manual setup →\n47\tquit from tray → confirm no leftover `java`/`python` processes → relaunch reuses\n48\t`%APPDATA%/<app>/benny-home`.\n49\t\n50\t## 2. Release (tagged, all platforms via CI)\n51\t\n52\t```\n53\t# 1. make sure everything is committed to main\n54\tgit status\n55\t# 2. bump version (writes package.json, creates the vX.Y.Z tag/commit)\n56\tnode scripts/manage-release.js [patch|minor|major]\n57\t# 3. push main FIRST, then the tag\n58\tgit push origin main\n59\tgit push origin vX.Y.Z\n60\t# 4. CI builds all 6 platforms and publishes the GitHub release (~30 min)\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t**CRITICAL ordering lesson:** always push `main` **before** the tag. If the tag arrives\n64\tfirst, the build jobs are skipped and the release ships empty. (This has bitten releases\n65\tbefore.)\n66\t\n67\tCI workflows in `.github/workflows/`:\n68\t- `release-desktop.yml` — builds Windows/macOS/Linux × x64/arm64 on tag push, publishes.\n69\t- `snapshot-build.yml` — auto-build on every commit (smoke).\n70\t\n71\t### Release gates (run before tagging)\n72\t```\n73\tpytest tests/release -q            # 6σ acceptance gates\n74\tpytest tests/portability -q        # SR-1: no absolute paths in manifests/config\n75\t```\n76\tPast failure mode: a release that shipped a broken NSIS build (no x64 installer / bad\n77\tarm64). Prefer a **slim bundle + build guard**; do a `desktop:localtest` and actually\n78\tlaunch the exe before tagging.\n79\t\n80\t## 3. Open-Studio companion services (Phase 5)\n81\t\n82\tThe desktop tray can drive the two OSS tools folded in by Open-Studio (see\n83\t`OPEN-STUDIO.md`). Logic in `packaging/desktop/openstudio_services.js`, wired into\n84\t`tray.js`:\n85\t- **opencode** — \"Start/Stop opencode server\" (`opencode serve`), shown only when the\n86\t  `opencode` CLI is on PATH.\n87\t- **open-notebook** — \"Start/Stop open-notebook (docker)\" + \"Open Notebook UI\"\n88\t  (`http://localhost:8502`), shown only when `docker` is on PATH. Drives\n89\t  `docker compose -f <file> up -d/down`.\n90\t- **Per-install secret:** `ensureEncryptionKey()` generates a random\n91\t  `OPEN_NOTEBOOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY` once and persists it in the desktop config, exporting it\n92\t  into the compose child env — replacing the hardcoded `=benny` from the sample compose.\n93\t- `stopAllOpenStudioServices()` is called from `prepareDesktopForQuit()` (stops opencode\n94\t  serve; leaves the docker stack, which may be shared).\n95\t\n96\tTo bundle these tools into the installer itself (future), extend\n97\t`packaging/runtime-bundle/` + `packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js` the same way the\n98\tBenny runtime is bundled.\n99\t\n100\t## Quick reference\n101\t\n102\t```\n103\tnpm run install:packaging          # one-time: electron/electron-builder\n104\tnpm run desktop:pack               # fast unpacked test build (shell only)\n105\tnpm run desktop:localtest          # zero-install full-runtime test build\n106\tnpm run package:desktop:windows    # Windows installer\n107\tnode scripts/manage-release.js patch && git push origin main && git push origin vX.Y.Z\n108\tpytest tests/release -q            # release gates\n109\t```\n110\t\n111\tRelated docs: `DEVOPS.md` (release narrative), `QUICKSTART-EXE.md` (operator setup),\n112\t`OPEN-STUDIO.md` (the integration this pipeline ships).\n113\t"}]},"uuid":"68839bd5-1009-4238-a96c-bd35da64c2bc","timestamp":"2026-06-20T14:33:58.795Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\.claude\\skills\\devops-pipeline\\SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: devops-pipeline\ndescription: Build, test-package, and release the Prime-Silo desktop app (Space Agent). Use when asked to build the app, make a local/test build, package for Windows/macOS/Linux, cut a release, bump the version, or debug the release CI. Covers the Open-Studio companion services (opencode + open-notebook) bundling.\n---\n\n# Prime-Silo DevOps pipeline\n\nPrime-Silo packages as an Electron desktop app (\"Space Agent\") via **electron-builder**.\nTwo product layers ship together: the Space-Agent shell (Node server + browser UI, run\nin-process) and the **Benny runtime** (Python + Neo4j + JRE) which is either bundled\n(zero-install) or driven from an external `$BENNY_HOME`.\n\nAll commands run from the repo root: `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo`.\n\n## 0. One-time: install packaging deps\n\nelectron + electron-builder live under `packaging/`. If `packaging/node_modules` is\nmissing, run first:\n```\nnpm run install:packaging\n```\n\n## 1. Build types (pick the lightest that proves what you need)\n\n| Goal | Command | Output | Notes |\n|------|---------|--------|------|\n| Fast shell-only test (validates main/tray/pet/UI changes) | `npm run desktop:pack` | `dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe` | **No** runtime bundle. Quick. Best for verifying desktop/main-process changes. |\n| Zero-install local test (full runtime) | `npm run desktop:localtest` | same path, with bundled Python+Neo4j+JRE | Sets `PRIME_SILO_BUNDLE_RUNTIME=1`; **downloads hundreds of MB + runs pip** — slow first run. This is the artifact to validate before tagging. |\n| Windows installer | `npm run package:desktop:windows` | NSIS installer in `dist/` | Full build. |\n| All Windows arches | `npm run package:desktop:windows:all` | x64 + arm64 | |\n| macOS / Linux | `npm run package:desktop:{macos,linux}[:all]` | dmg+zip / AppImage | Run on the target OS. |\n\nBuild internals: scripts under `packaging/scripts/` (`host-package.js`,\n`build-local-test.js` → `desktop-builder.js`). `build.files` in `package.json` controls\nwhat ships — `packaging/desktop/**/*` is globbed, so new files there (e.g. `pet.js`,\n`openstudio_services.js`) bundle automatically. `app/L1` and `app/L2` are excluded.\n\n### Verify a build\n```\nls \"dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe\"\n# asar is disabled, so app files are browsable for spot-checks:\nls \"dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/resources/app/packaging/desktop/\"\n```\nFor a zero-install build, follow the on-screen checklist `build-local-test.js` prints:\nlaunch the exe → tray reaches **\"Benny runtime: running (bundled)\"** → in the Bridge,\nDocuments ingest + Code 3D graph + Flows deep-produce all work with no manual setup →\nquit from tray → confirm no leftover `java`/`python` processes → relaunch reuses\n`%APPDATA%/<app>/benny-home`.\n\n## 2. Release (tagged, all platforms via CI)\n\n```\n# 1. make sure everything is committed to main\ngit status\n# 2. bump version (writes package.json, creates the vX.Y.Z tag/commit)\nnode scripts/manage-release.js [patch|minor|major]\n# 3. push main FIRST, then the tag\ngit push origin main\ngit push origin vX.Y.Z\n# 4. CI builds all 6 platforms and publishes the GitHub release (~30 min)\n```\n\n**CRITICAL ordering lesson:** always push `main` **before** the tag. If the tag arrives\nfirst, the build jobs are skipped and the release ships empty. (This has bitten releases\nbefore.)\n\nCI workflows in `.github/workflows/`:\n- `release-desktop.yml` — builds Windows/macOS/Linux × x64/arm64 on tag push, publishes.\n- `snapshot-build.yml` — auto-build on every commit (smoke).\n\n### Release gates (run before tagging)\n```\npytest tests/release -q            # 6σ acceptance gates\npytest tests/portability -q        # SR-1: no absolute paths in manifests/config\n```\nPast failure mode: a release that shipped a broken NSIS build (no x64 installer / bad\narm64). Prefer a **slim bundle + build guard**; do a `desktop:localtest` and actually\nlaunch the exe before tagging.\n\n## 3. Open-Studio companion services (Phase 5)\n\nThe desktop tray can drive the two OSS tools folded in by Open-Studio (see\n`OPEN-STUDIO.md`). Logic in `packaging/desktop/openstudio_services.js`, wired into\n`tray.js`:\n- **opencode** — \"Start/Stop opencode server\" (`opencode serve`), shown only when the\n  `opencode` CLI is on PATH.\n- **open-notebook** — \"Start/Stop open-notebook (docker)\" + \"Open Notebook UI\"\n  (`http://localhost:8502`), shown only when `docker` is on PATH. Drives\n  `docker compose -f <file> up -d/down`.\n- **Per-install secret:** `ensureEncryptionKey()` generates a random\n  `OPEN_NOTEBOOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY` once and persists it in the desktop config, exporting it\n  into the compose child env — replacing the hardcoded `=benny` from the sample compose.\n- `stopAllOpenStudioServices()` is called from `prepareDesktopForQuit()` (stops opencode\n  serve; leaves the docker stack, which may be shared).\n\nTo bundle these tools into the installer itself (future), extend\n`packaging/runtime-bundle/` + `packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js` the same way the\nBenny runtime is bundled.\n\n## Quick reference\n\n```\nnpm run install:packaging          # one-time: electron/electron-builder\nnpm run desktop:pack     