{"parentUuid":"75703263-af66-4cd4-a93e-1749f839adc6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014BVBu6wewKE62Bj5Y9t82J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investigated and fixed. Here's the root cause and what I changed.\n\n## Root cause — a frontend gap, not a bug in ingestion\n\nThe \"2 awaiting ingestion\" number was **correct** — it's `pendingCount`, the files whose status isn't `ALIGNED` (i.e. not yet indexed). The real problem is there was **no way to act on it per-file**:\n\n- The Documents file list rendered each file as a **read-only row** (name + status) — no checkbox, no per-file button.\n- The single **\"Ingest → triples\"** button called `ingest()`, which posted `{workspace, deep_synthesis:true}` with **no `files` list**.\n- The backend ([`rag_routes.py:100`](prime-silo/runtime/benny/api/rag_routes.py)) then falls into the `else` branch and **globs everything** in `data_in`:\n  ```python\n  if request.files: file_paths = [data_in_path / f for f in request.files]\n  else:             file_paths = list(data_in_path.glob(\"*.*\"))   # ← all of them\n  ```\n\nSo the backend *already* supported ingesting a chosen subset (`IngestRequest.files: List[str]`) — the UI just never sent it. It was all-or-nothing because the frontend never offered a selection.\n\n## The fix (frontend only — backend was already capable)\n\n- [`bridge.js`](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js): added `selectedFiles[]` state, `reconcileSelection()` (called from `loadFiles` — prunes files that vanished and **pre-selects anything still awaiting ingestion**, so \"ingest the doc I just added\" is one click; already-ingested files stay unchecked so re-ingest is deliberate), plus `isSelected / toggleFile / selectAllFiles / clearFileSelection`. `ingest()` now sends `files: <selected names>` and refuses to run with nothing selected (otherwise an empty list would make the backend glob everything again).\n- [`view.html`](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/view.html): a **checkbox per file**, a **Select all / None** bar, a live header count (`… · N selected`), and the button now reads **\"Ingest selected (N)\"** and is disabled at 0.\n- [`bridge.css`](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.css): styles for the checkbox row and the tools bar.\n\nValidated with `node --check`, and synced into both the installed app and the `win-unpacked` build's `resources/app`.\n\n## To test in the exe\nLaunch → Documents. You'll now see a checkbox on each row. Your 2 awaiting files will be **pre-ticked**; untick the one you don't want, and the button shows exactly how many you're ingesting. Re-ingesting an already-indexed file is safe — the backend deletes that source's old vectors first.\n\nThis is hot-synced for testing but **not committed/released**. When you're happy with both this and the adaptive-RAG change, say so and I'll commit and cut the next patch release together."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_read_input_tokens":170509,"output_tokens":1039,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":170509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcExRLEikDKipdwdvV5cc","type":"assistant","uuid":"d198d910-7734-4547-b628-658f04ded219","timestamp":"2026-06-20T18:06:46.351Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"50d606f7-67d3-4645-8504-2cafd7318b4d","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"rec